two boar attacks two very different  outcomes here's how a scene in house of  the dragon had fans thinking back to the  first season of game of thrones  much of the third episode of house of  the dragon revolves around a rather  pathetic royal stag hunt in the  kingswood and king viserys's troubles  regarding matters of family and  succession princess rhaenyra targaryen  is technically traveling with the king  but wants absolutely nothing to do with  the staged hunt let alone the clumsy and  self-serving social activities around it  making it even less appealing is lord  jason lannister of casterly rock who is  aspiring to win her hand in marriage  thank you for the wine  rhaenyra chooses to distance herself  from the proceedings by taking a ride in  the woods accompanied by her hand-picked  kingsguard member sir kristen cole their  stay in the forest ends up going on  quite a bit longer than anyone but  rhaenyra is comfortable with and even  includes a brief encounter with a  majestic stag that's markedly different  from viserys's experience but it's  another notable incident during rhaenyra  and sir kristen's forest jaunt that  brings an entirely different and much  later king to mind as princess rhaenyra  and sir kristen are hanging out in the  forest a mysterious noise from the  bushes prompts them to investigate the  source of the sound turns out to be an  extremely disgruntled wild boar which  charges kristen and sends the knight  flying the boar then attempts to attack  and gore ray nera but fortunately the  pair manages to kill the animal in the  nick of time game of thrones fans will  immediately remember another time a boar  attacked a royal in the woods king  robert baratheon is grievously wounded  when a boar attacks him during a hunting  expedition that also takes place in the  kingswood this is an incredibly  important event since robert's death  leads to the arrest and execution of ned  stark and sets the stage for the bloody  succession conflict that fuels the rest  of the series while there are obvious  similarities between the borah attacks  and house of the dragon and game of  thrones there are also very clear  differences the boar attack in game of  thrones is a highly shady affair as the  lannisters have made sure that robert  had plenty to drink the night before the  hunt the attack itself also happens off  screen between episodes as if to  underscore the highly underwhelming  nature of king robert's rule  my fault  too much wine  missed my thrust the boar scene in house  of the dragon happens fully on screen  and the end result of the terrifying  encounter couldn't be more different  either while robert dies a sad  contemplative death in bed while making  a hasty attempt to set his affairs in  order and right past wrongs rhaenyra  rides back to the hunting party with the  dead bore in tow looking more regal than  ever and drawing odd and admiring looks  from everyone who sees her the effect of  rhaenyra bagging a dangerous boar with  just one night is further enhanced by  the fact that many of the people present  just saw her father's bungling attempts  to put a stag out of its misery despite  the fact that people were literally  holding it for him to stab so when  robert meets zabor his rule and his life  comes to a pitiful end rhaenyra  encounters one and not only lives to  tell the tale but gains bucket loads of  respect that'll surely prove worth its  weight in gold going forward  [Music]
 

